<title>GERMANY: East German March industry orders rise 7.4 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>East German March industry orders rise 7.4 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS     Mar 97     Feb 97     Mar 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   +7.4	 +6.5	 -3.9</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +23.2	+10.1	-10.5</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		150.4	140.0	122.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted, provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details (mth-on-mth)</p>
<p>				  Mar 97    Feb 97    Mar 97 index</p>
<p> Domestic orders	     +1.1	+9.1	158.5</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Feb/Mar 97 with Dec/Jan 96/97:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		 +10.0</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Feb/Mar 97 with Feb/Mar 96:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		 +10.3</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 +2.3</p>
<p> Foreign orders			 +51.4</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		   +11.2</p>
<p> Capital goods			  +12.4</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    +1.0</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
